<title>SINGAPORE: ICB 1996 net profit rises 16.8 pct.</title>
<headline>ICB 1996 net profit rises 16.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>		    (in million S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		    80.58  vs    68.97</p>
<p>    Dividend  (cents)	    4.0   vs     4.0</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)	   47.9   vs    41.0</p>
<p>    Group Interest income    207.43  vs   173.11</p>
<p>    Group interest expense    84.02  vs    66.80</p>
<p>  Group net interest income  123.41  vs   106.32</p>
<p>  Group fees and commissions  12.30  vs    10.67</p>
<p>  Group dividends		  1.24  vs     1.85</p>
<p>  Other operating income	17.52  vs    13.60</p>
<p>  Tax				 28.29  vs    24.22</p>
<p>Minorities			 0.43  vs     0.93</p>
<p>  Parent net profit	     84.30  vs    72.24</p>
<p>  Parent interest income     206.38  vs   172.04</p>
<p>  Parent net interest income 122.21  vs   105.09</p>
<p>  Last Day Books Open	  June 5</p>
<p>  Dividend pay		   June 17</p>
<p>Note- Industrial &amp; Commercial Bank Ltd (ICB) is a subsidiary of United Overseas Bank Group.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
